	)
	(text "TODO: U11 is referenced to \nDIG_PRE_GND so its output will \nbe offset by the drop across \nR28 (Rsense). For example at\nI=20mA Rsense will have a drop of 2mV\nand U11 will output 20mV; however, \nthis is referenced to DIG_PRE_GND which is\n2mV lower than DIGITAL_GND and so will\nbe read as 18mV.\nLikewise with 1Amp, Rsense will drop 100mV,\nU11 will output 1V but referenced to \nDIG_PRE_GND which will be 100mV lower than \nDIGITAL_GND and so will be read as 900mV.\nI might want to skip this circuit here and put\na dedicated fuel guage chip into the battery \nenclosure."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.868 122.174 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a9719d5f-e4af-4224-9b79-b1363f657114")
	)
	(text "ERC overrides"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 120.142 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a98b6625-9490-422e-93a0-25bb47fe405f")
	)
	(text "Need a 3.7V to 5V boost converter for battery\npower, and a 3.7V Li Ion battery charger. \nStill not sure on how much power we need for\ncloudy day and overnight operation but we can \nprobably size the battery later. \nActually, I think we'll add a separate battery\ncircuit as its own thing. It will be self-contained\nand all we need here are a couple of lines to \nprovide battery power and return and a current shunt\nfor battery monitoring. I think maybe I'll also include \nthe battery shunt and amplifier in the battery module. \nThis just means we need a +/- and sense pin for the battery\nmodule.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.608 -14.224 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c617f0a3-6728-4868-a272-165699edb34b")
	)
